diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..7f65e26 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,48 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Sign-in supports a passkey button, conditional passkey autofill, and the existing
+password service. Sign-up creates an account through that service, establishes a
+session, then offers optional passkey enrollment. `/devtools-times/account` provides
+passkey creation, names, registration/last-used dates, removal, display-name changes,
+identity verification, and sign-out. Passwords remain available as a recovery method,
+including after removing the last passkey. Passwords and biometric data are never
+stored by this application.
+
+The auth API uses native WebAuthn in the browser, `webauthn-polyfills` for JSON and
+capability support, and [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server)
+for server-side attestation/signature verification. HttpOnly sessions, one-time
+session-bound challenges (5 minutes), origin checks, credential ownership checks,
+and recent verification (5 minutes) protect account changes. Reauthentication
+requires user verification and restricts allowed credentials to the current user.
+Browser password-manager synchronization is best effort and feature detected.
+
+Deployment configuration:
+
+- Use **Node.js 24+**. Authentication persistence uses built-in `node:sqlite`.
+- Set `WEBAUTHN_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin, without a path, such as
+  `https://news.example.com`. This determines the expected WebAuthn origin, RP ID,
+  allowed POST origin, and Secure cookie flag. The default is the origin in
+  `astro.config.mjs`; localhost uses the request's local origin for development.
+  Credentials are bound to this domain, so keep it stable.
+- Set `AUTH_DB_PATH` to a writable persistent SQLite file. The default is
+  `./.data/auth.sqlite` (gitignored). Back up this file and keep it across deployments.
+  The included store supports a single deployment with persistent local storage;
+  replicas on separate filesystems need a shared database implementation. The
+  existing external password service remains the authority for usernames/passwords.
+- Account routes and the session cookie respect Astro's configured base path.
+  The existing password service must be reachable from the server.
+
+Provider names and small icons are a checked-in snapshot of the
+[community AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids)
+(retrieved October 28, 2026). AAGUID metadata only provides display hints. Unknown
+providers and larger omitted icons use the generic key icon.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for request-level cryptographic/authentication tests (in-memory SQLite,
+mocked password service, no server or browser), `pnpm check:auth` for focused auth
+TypeScript checks, and `pnpm build` for the application build. Whole-project
+`tsc --noEmit` currently also reports existing errors in `MenuButton.tsx` and
+`src/utils/images.ts`.
